\begin_layout Standard
The code solves
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{H}(\boldsymbol{r})\ket{\Psi^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})}=\varepsilon^{\lambda}\ket{\Psi^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})}
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{\Psi(\boldsymbol{r})}$
\end_inset

 is an 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

-component vector
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\ket{\Psi^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})}=\begin{pmatrix}\Psi_{1}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})\\
\vdots\\
\Psi_{n}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})
\end{pmatrix}
\]

\end_inset

while the Hamiltonian is
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{H}(\boldsymbol{r})=\begin{pmatrix}(-\i\nabla-\boldsymbol{A})^{2}+H_{11}(\boldsymbol{r})-\i\Gamma_{1} & H_{21}(\boldsymbol{r}) & \cdots\\
H_{12}(\boldsymbol{r}) & (-\i\nabla-\boldsymbol{A})^{2}+H_{22}(\boldsymbol{r})-\i\Gamma_{2} & \cdots\\
\vdots & \vdots & \ddots
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

\end_inset

Presently,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{A}$
\end_inset

 can only be the same for all states.
 If 
\family typewriter
A_x
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
A_y
\family default
 are passed,
 they are used for all states.
 If they are passed as 
\family typewriter
nothing
\family default
,
 then only the Laplace is used:
 
\begin_inset Formula $(-\i\nabla-\boldsymbol{A})^{2}\to-\Delta$
\end_inset

.
 The functions 
\begin_inset Formula $H_{ij}(\boldsymbol{r})$
\end_inset

 are passed in the 
\family typewriter
H
\family default
 matrix.
 Constants 
\begin_inset Formula $\Gamma_{i}$
\end_inset

 are passed in the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathtt{\Gamma}$
\end_inset

 array.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The orthonormality of eigenvectors is expressed as
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\intop\d\boldsymbol{r}\,\braket{\Psi^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})}{\Psi^{\mu}(\boldsymbol{r})}=\intop\d\boldsymbol{r}\,\sum_{i}\Psi_{i}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})\Psi_{i}^{\mu}(\boldsymbol{r})=\delta^{\lambda\mu}.
\]

\end_inset

Note that the functions 
\begin_inset Formula $\Psi_{i}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})$
\end_inset

 for different 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

's need not be orthogonal,
 i.e.
 there is no requirement for 
\begin_inset Formula $\intop\d\boldsymbol{r}\,\Psi_{i}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})\Psi_{j}^{\lambda}(\boldsymbol{r})$
\end_inset

 to be proportional to 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta_{ij}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

